<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37754" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξωρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>untimely, out of season, unfitting,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξωρα πράσσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					618
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>too late, too old, superannuated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				1.95
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sull.</u>
				36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Herm.</u>
				78
			</span></i>, al. (also glossed by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξαέτης</span> as though <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕξωρος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				350.2
			</span></i>): c. gen., <i>too old for . .,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ἐρᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Merc.Cond.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ρως, ἔχειν τοῦ ἀποδημεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					1.21.8
				</span></i>
			.</div>
